module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleEventualGeneration.Affine
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmplePowers.TensorPowerAmple
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleLocalGeneration.Basic

/-!
# Clause (7) of Stacks Tag 01Q3 from local generation after a twist

Clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] has two halves:
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsEventuallyFinGenPowers`, that the powers of `L` are eventually
generated by finitely many global sections, and
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist`, that every quasi-coherent module of
finite type is generated by finitely many global sections after some twist. This file proves that
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`, the module-valued form of
[Stacks, Tag 01PW], implies both halves for an ample invertible module `L`, once it holds for `L`
and for every positive tensor power of `L`. Clause (8) follows.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen.tensor_tensorPow_add` and
  `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen.tensor_tensorPow_add_mul`: a generated twist of `F`
  stays generated when the degree is increased by a degree in which the twisting module is itself
  generated, and hence by any nonnegative multiple of one.
* `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.exists_nat_isFinGen_tensor_tensorPow`: the twist of
  `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist` may be taken nonnegative, given a
  positive degree in which the twisting module is generated.
* `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`:
  the first half of clause (7) for the powers of `L`.
* `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`:
  clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3], for an ample invertible module.
* `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isQuotientOfNegativeTwists_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`:
  clause (8) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3], for an ample invertible module.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist` quantifies its twist over `ℤ`, while
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_forall_exists_pow` asks for one in
`ℕ`, since it identifies `(L ^⊗ d) ^⊗ k` with `L ^⊗ (d k)` through
`Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.tensorPowModulePowIso`, which exists only for a nonnegative outer
exponent.

The hypothesis is asked for at `L` itself and at every positive power:
`Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule X L 1` is only isomorphic to `L`, and
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist` has no transport along an isomorphism
of the twisting module.

The hypothesis holds for every ample invertible module, by
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isAmple`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EBD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EBD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory
open Stacks.Ample AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules

universe u

namespace Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Raising the twist -/

/-- **Raising the degree of a generated twist.** If `F ⊗ P ^⊗ a` is generated by finitely many
global sections and so is `P ^⊗ b`, then so is `F ⊗ P ^⊗ (a + b)`. This is
[Stacks, Tag 01AO] for an invertible factor. -/
theorem IsFinGen.tensor_tensorPow_add {F P : X.Modules} [IsInvertibleModule X P] {a b c : ℤ}
    (h : a + b = c) (ha : IsFinGen (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X P a))
    (hb : IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X P b)) : IsFinGen (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X P c) :=
  (ha.tensor hb).of_iso (Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.tensorPowShift (L := P) F h)

/-- **Raising the degree of a generated twist by a multiple.** If `F ⊗ P ^⊗ a` and `P ^⊗ t` are
generated by finitely many global sections, then so is `F ⊗ P ^⊗ (a + t r)` for every `r : ℕ`. -/
theorem IsFinGen.tensor_tensorPow_add_mul {F P : X.Modules} [IsInvertibleModule X P] {a t : ℤ}
    (ha : IsFinGen (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X P a)) (ht : IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X P t)) :
    ∀ r : ℕ, IsFinGen (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X P (a + t * r)) := by
  intro r
  induction r with
  | zero => simpa using ha
  | succ r ih =>
      exact IsFinGen.tensor_tensorPow_add (a := a + t * r) (b := t) (by push_cast; ring) ih ht

/-- **The twist may be taken nonnegative.** If `P ^⊗ t` is generated by finitely many global
sections for some `t ≥ 1` and `P` satisfies
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist`, then every quasi-coherent `F` of finite
type has `F ⊗ P ^⊗ k` generated by finitely many global sections for some `k : ℕ`. -/
theorem exists_nat_isFinGen_tensor_tensorPow {P : X.Modules} [IsInvertibleModule X P] {t : ℤ}
    (ht1 : 1 ≤ t) (ht : IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X P t))
    (h : IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist X P) (F : X.Modules) (hF : F.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hFt : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, IsFinGen (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X P (k : ℤ)) := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := h F hF hFt
  have hnn : 0 ≤ m + t * (m.natAbs : ℤ) := by
    have := le_mul_of_one_le_left (Int.natCast_nonneg m.natAbs) ht1
    omega
  refine ⟨(m + t * (m.natAbs : ℤ)).toNat, ?_⟩
  rw [Int.toNat_of_nonneg hnn]
  exact hm.tensor_tensorPow_add_mul ht m.natAbs

/-! ### Half (1) from the residual of half (2) -/

/-- **The first half of clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] from the residual of the second half.**
If every positive tensor power of an ample `L` satisfies
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`, then the powers of `L` are generated
by finitely many global sections in every sufficiently positive degree. -/
theorem isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist (L : X.Modules)
    [IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : IsAmple X L)
    (H : ∀ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d → Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X
      (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ))) :
    IsEventuallyFinGenPowers X L := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd1, hdgen⟩ := Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule L hL
  have hL' : IsAmple X (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ)) :=
    Stacks.AmplePowers.isAmple_tensorPowModule_of_isAmple L d hd1 hL
  have h2' : IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist X (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ)) :=
    Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist
      X (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ)) hL' (H d hd1)
  obtain ⟨t, ht1, ht⟩ := Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_pos_isFinGen_tensorPowModule
    (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ)) hL'
  refine isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_forall_exists_pow (d := (d : ℤ)) (by omega) hdgen fun j => ?_
  exact exists_nat_isFinGen_tensor_tensorPow (by omega) ht h2' (tensorPowModule X L j)
    (Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_tensorPowModule L j)
    (isFiniteType_of_isInvertibleModule _)

/-! ### Clause (7) and clause (8) -/

/-- **Clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] for a quasi-compact scheme with an ample invertible module,
from one residual.** If `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist` holds for `L`
and for each of its positive tensor powers, then every finite-type quasi-coherent module becomes
generated by finitely many global sections after every sufficiently positive twist by `L`. -/
theorem isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist (L : X.Modules)
    [IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : IsAmple X L)
    (H : ∀ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d → Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X
      (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ)))
    (H₀ : Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X L) :
    Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.IsEventuallyGloballyGenerated X L :=
  isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isEventuallyFinGenPowers
    (isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist L hL H)
    (Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist
      X L hL H₀)

/-- **Clause (8) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] from the same residual**: every finite-type quasi-coherent
module is a quotient of a finite direct sum of negative tensor powers of `L` of arbitrarily
negative degree, with quasi-coherent kernel. -/
theorem isQuotientOfNegativeTwists_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist (L : X.Modules)
    [IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : IsAmple X L)
    (H : ∀ d : ℕ, 1 ≤ d → Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X
      (tensorPowModule X L (d : ℤ)))
    (H₀ : Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X L) :
    Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.IsQuotientOfNegativeTwists X L :=
  Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuotientOfNegativeTwists_of_isEventuallyGloballyGenerated
    (isEventuallyGloballyGenerated_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist L hL H H₀)

end Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration

end
